"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011026","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7ba06c876d87a6324f9ae9ab0b2c2621fc44db366ee43d5279dd6498c7dd74ac","compact":"79501234b292c8b3a3877f3c1a6bd1be060fc2f4326d7352a918728f340f9921","nasal":"79501234b292c8b3a3877f3c1a6bd1be060fc2f4326d7352a918728f340f9921"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-27","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":27,"english":"You are of truthful vows, heroic, pious, of firm prowess, discriminating, recollecting and having implicit confidence in your friends.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.781,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011027","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d1acaa584360c3eb09544c660a4dd72f869634dcc930122b0bc6d836b0e6448c","compact":"5975cf6871982d87b16434c6f1718a787ab71ae9d6d1a51e29e001a0dd099e9e","nasal":"9f4d35f318d1c783f1cc9f6ebc9a0643d3f8f407060e78571d7d52ccc3899591"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-28","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":28,"english":"Let the intelligent and capable counsellors deliver their reasonable opinions to you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.778,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011028","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8cd9dee8959402db071026df098a87cca19212a79d269e415e8affd35bd612c6","compact":"81b43978a772718c0e4db294661c38853b106c07d8916a390b5e8fb365654ed2","nasal":"b6f6b1344b06a2103f3214cc3c8e10450c6d107f851dbde948b666820fe3885b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-29","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":29,"english":"They speaking thus to Rāghava, the intelligent monkey Angada, spoke as follows for sounding the intention of Vibhīşaņa.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-36"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011029","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3edca95aa196648d44dd195c27f6da5e621b4e44b605ca9bf089a6d81742f696","compact":"2a241c4a5accd0e13d4d19a154e46b902e8124e201f2b5d51ba8958638041bd6","nasal":"9346a109c5eb5eb145ff1d79a45c4f7d177d2115210b1d69fac7c9c8804f8587"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-30","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":30,"english":"We should always suspect him since he has come from the side of our enemies, and should not, all on a sudden, place confidence in him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.631,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-37"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011030","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cde6f9b56c06be0d35b70a4ab2d40f10cf17421ae9d0bbaf900bb7e844a851a0","compact":"c7bdd2d38a5ea78ac0e503fbf2e0713a52373fb256458a3951d6e9413f92c386","nasal":"c2da577556f975e941af6f6ef981cbd7a4e42d02fdb379f6cf8da2ab9c41ae80"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-31","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":31,"english":"The wicked-minded always move about hiding their real self, and bring about peoples' calamity, taking advantage of their weak points. And great is the disaster thereof.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-38"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011031","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"36fec5889cfc39972142b42678561564937f0a4de55577ea79e6a7d032af7d6c","compact":"cf251b45b81914639f78e650a97a973172876e4cbc1574e0e0229294f0013bcb","nasal":"3704eb61cdbcd034ef20ffbd9097eec5ca6b1e14030c8602d0ba6c97da5ac96c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-32","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":32,"english":"It is always proper to engage in actions, considering what is right and what is wrong. Virtues should always be gathered and vices abondoned.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.846,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-39"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011032","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"734ff1ac932d3abf8b197d52d0aa47984b050306f729122c57eacd855afdbc45","compact":"e52a80a1d5a764d9d3b21642c0e7f331ad980d4b75ad1382387046e84678b9f9","nasal":"e52a80a1d5a764d9d3b21642c0e7f331ad980d4b75ad1382387046e84678b9f9"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-33","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":33,"english":"Do you renounce him unhesitatingly, if did you find in him a source of a great calamity and do you embrace him if did you find him crowned with many virtues.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.892,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-40"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011033","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9aba58067177441f35cdccc442a293abde3f701100b2b364ae100ab2c9428a54","compact":"f1a4628b707d754f3d00f55581398be546fb7dbfa43c9e17fd9ccdd3e21b96c3","nasal":"a0b9115f4b9355578b2e2886f67e6a35ccb77d6cf00706165944571269df8fc2"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-34","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":34,"english":"There upon followed Sarava with words fraught with high import, best of men, do you speedily despatch emissaries to sound Vibhis ana.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-41"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011034","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"59d0ad13c2fd86b173e907001137f852330722b4330918fc33862ea8be2fd98a","compact":"dd6e8ba869dc65c57ae7b248c3e3641d5cafb4f99656b8d9d15d8395a1fb96ba","nasal":"9aa1f2d3ea77397960fdb554b5f19fedbc6ba56a4af75fc4c311a7e69a75c063"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-35","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":35,"english":"If did you, sounding him well through the instrumentality of sharp spies, find him friendly, do you win him over to your side.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.891,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-42"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011035","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"58e64f1f6e7f795744366f2a72463258dcc6ae6de711ea38ef9424ab45821058","compact":"3cd1c59b21687f7b985f45016fb6006fcb5b63544ef3c5ba463e352472e67383","nasal":"3cd1c59b21687f7b985f45016fb6006fcb5b63544ef3c5ba463e352472e67383"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-36","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":36,"english":"There upon the wise Jāmbavān, arriving at conclusions by virtue of his knowledge of Šāstras, began with words, void of defects.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-43"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011036","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"af887e60d686b6270e59fe84847a8c60be0fda4149dc7f7af42e2b8a296a01cd","compact":"b43280b042c25ec7b9a4bfe616f40cf41e0d6263b072a11a219ca7d689237918","nasal":"52f67d72f6ccda9f92d3c4c6837079e3146c980d843c04c4099e4a7c9cbc9150"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-37","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":37,"english":"Surely does Vibhīşaņa come from the vicious lord of Räkşasas, dead set against us and has arrived at such a bad piace and in such a bad hour. We should always fear him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.884,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-44"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011037","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"edc56a8b7bff66d06f1feaf83c03276d62506d9b9362105850ed55e894eed0e6","compact":"0bbeb926dad797207bb025c74924e62af474f3b97212130caddb57f590b9bb9d","nasal":"ecb1a0c93c81cb3e60a593f1c8e51e91130aa335f9b7e358846fb7a37ec2aaeb"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-38","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":38,"english":"There upon followed Mainda, conversant with what is right and wrong, after due deliberation, with words pregnant with words pregnant with reason.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.9,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-45"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011038","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0342a4d0ad16b2f3f9b41ea8cd5d8bc03909b31930a3303a2e07c1201149aec8","compact":"dff1afa204be989ceeed56be319df9223197c0b675b89f4b6c01fcbdf8420d9f","nasal":"387bee8d30bd289db9d8e4dc7fbc57b921448bd2a076b5e5ce4ec7c5371366b7"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-39","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":39,"english":"He is Rāvana's younger brother, by name Vibhīşana. Let the lord of men ask him every thing at first in sweet words.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.792,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-46"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011039","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f837b7d5516434511836e9aa718eb3ed1f22153f77542f181a01202cb43277e2","compact":"23779cc992225fe0dd47f570de1c7651ce869c18ef49baa0db367ca3e603a1b3","nasal":"23779cc992225fe0dd47f570de1c7651ce869c18ef49baa0db367ca3e603a1b3"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-40","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":40,"english":"Do you first ascertain, O foremost of men, with what intention he has come evil or good and then settle what course to adopt.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.703,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-47"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011040","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2dfcf20f16d0a7c3aa9459533f161f80e412065a9f8fcca37d4750d12ea56a4f","compact":"b7f7fea189cbf2939820a1845d11506f98aeca74db3150d377dd549939fdec0f","nasal":"b7f7fea189cbf2939820a1845d11506f98aeca74db3150d377dd549939fdec0f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-41","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":41,"english":"There upon spoke Hanumān, the foremost of the counsellors and well versed in Šāstras, in accents sweet, glorious and fraught with a high value.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.825,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-48"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011041","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1231ec626fa07be2ea8b0fc8cb76e1188fc617da8d54b777ed009eb89db4387c","compact":"cf2dce35f11be9d7566ff25bcd114cde7eedda2ee8b673168a0fb6c9795f3a87","nasal":"4ea5962081939dc7dcacf90afe94782e4ebb0c6900b97ba86d5c98c6492e71d7"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-42","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":42,"english":"Even Brhaspati, (the lord of speech) cannot excel you, capaable,* gifted with the best of intellect and foremost of those skilled in the are of speech, as you are. *Capable to ascertain the truth of all Sastras.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-49"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011042","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a273c2c276a9d50fc26add257a0679de20837dd7600613bc36799010dfe6b77f","compact":"310113f503d124592a90695d328f85e66b875b0a3fb110b813a90993d98d613a","nasal":"f066b572dce2a6a5e673a2ff47fe26d7c7f8f0b397cb8868df72209fc1f0f010"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-43","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":43,"english":"And what I know I speak, o king. I do so, in the interest of Rāma's work and not impelled by my skill in the are of speech, by the pride of being a counsellor, by the vanity of being gifted with a high intellect or by the desire of speaking for its own sake.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.754,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-50"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011043","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"00b5bb23de95afa97301d0ee3ff9fc2ca64710d0f9547427e0f6f6905c9a304f","compact":"1ed822a8be59ab950bdd7840f2f8d51aa6d9cc576c63db953d362dd96d310cdc","nasal":"3d036fcd967dea58aec62fe5e19b2b5a8d6ea0eb1e62a0cb19aeafbdd95592ac"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-44","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":44,"english":"What your counsellors have said for ascertaining the good or evil intention of Vibhīş aņa appear to me as most defective and productive of no consequence whatever. It is impossible to sound him without any command.* *To command to relate for what he has come.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-51"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011044","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ffdeb586ccdbe6fc0e19bf943c2e46bb115216fcc9f98bf0c3396788d5200cde","compact":"045fc712873b6efb82107cf7eeda840027ac635172bbc1a20c747990cee66204","nasal":"045fc712873b6efb82107cf7eeda840027ac635172bbc1a20c747990cee66204"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-45","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":45,"english":"And even to command him now for the same appears to me as improper.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.733,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-52"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011045","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3963be9f7afce10531ec1a037eccd27c472d540b8cacc53b573c3ee555006f2c","compact":"0916be46e9edf3f964cf81f4608f91e7b62b445a25e995629e4ff0a942645b08","nasal":"0916be46e9edf3f964cf81f4608f91e7b62b445a25e995629e4ff0a942645b08"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-46","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":46,"english":"And as regards the despatch of spies, anent what you have been advised by your ministers, I do not observe any utility.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-53"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011046","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bda62e1d8fb127323a80c469ed029344b8e356e895575e7a6160c79578f37179","compact":"9afa3f1552c5912c17ad46db81c49820329fe15d0ee27b8e75e4598912d2d76d","nasal":"9afa3f1552c5912c17ad46db81c49820329fe15d0ee27b8e75e4598912d2d76d"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-47","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":47,"english":"And what little I have thought of, I have something to say (regarding Jambaban's proposal) that Vibhīşaņa has arrived at such a bad place and in such an evil hour.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.717,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-54"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011047","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2e088ea42f78028676a4bf3800c4b244c0883ae87e9d8473a2e6cf54fce3c077","compact":"1b34d9bafd5c3852d2af94a8473bf47f87e566f2f0a710bf785004bb0d105c65","nasal":"1b34d9bafd5c3852d2af94a8473bf47f87e566f2f0a710bf785004bb0d105c65"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-48","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":48,"english":"He has really come to a very good place and in a very good hour. And truly has he performed a becoming and sensille action by coming here after duly ascertaining that Rāvana is a vicious wight and you are a pious person-he is full of vices-you are gifted with many virtues-he is tyrannical and you are powerful.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.863,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-55"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011048","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e700b709c8b8ee13bc896d7ff7a06b2152cef9cfa54a673d87c9f72b135542fc","compact":"2aa16165d9bafc95c7b0056f8dcac1ada80a923bf6353afa6d25795fd2cc4250","nasal":"2aa16165d9bafc95c7b0056f8dcac1ada80a923bf6353afa6d25795fd2cc4250"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-49","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":49,"english":"He has really come to a very good place and in a very good hour. And truly has he performed a becoming and sensille action by coming here after duly ascertaining that Rāvana is a vicious wight and you are a pious person-he is full of vices-you are gifted with many virtues-he is tyrannical and you are powerful.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.828,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-55"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011049","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c87c7ec52ce3d2ff68fcbba28cea680a569cc5fe39b40f15287943a6b91025e0","compact":"fec9e61900a59878d77dadab8bccea10ccda492af814c3236147dd1421ffcce8","nasal":"fec9e61900a59878d77dadab8bccea10ccda492af814c3236147dd1421ffcce8"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-50","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":50,"english":"And what they have said, O king, as regards sounding him through secret spies, appear to me as one requiring great wisdom.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-56"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011050","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"51cef1d41dcd2d667278ca8c5e0e40a7eade0396a8a7e064b90d1ad8b1219c7c","compact":"ba2cd4b83146962b8a64e7230e254799955749e8369f21ec6cee19b36c533cf4","nasal":"ba2cd4b83146962b8a64e7230e254799955749e8369f21ec6cee19b36c533cf4"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-51","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":51,"english":"An intelligent man, when questioned by any suddenly, suspects many things. And if the newcomer be a friend and has come here for his own happiness, how greatly shall his mind be changed by such a course?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.809,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-57"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011051","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"879338c740207f9cfbe9da804bd573af470561f11df5226cc2d4a468e77434b3","compact":"96f56302823de9b26def3895cb64840e4c71a91b21cb121a7e4af211d2e17f46","nasal":"243f3098cf6efc3239e8bba84fde7f6ca6551a4f7318b0804ec8698b4a3f8a1c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-52","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":52,"english":"Besides by a sudden questioning it is impossible to ascertain the intention of a foreigner. Do you therefore yourself accost him and determine, by his voice, his secret motive.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.275,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-58"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011052","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"47afe28dd7bd18e01b385a51288191d745d0c79a2cee0a6fc056091225006a56","compact":"e0d5104ac04eeb260a48a20054c584a0f216da9ece295ea54bfb4425104407b0","nasal":"c5a642c08f631a95409284281f9d3c84bacf33fc47a5c71b259af13dda79a227"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-53","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":53,"english":"I did not however mark anything of his wickedness while he spoke; rather I did observe signs of gladness on his countenance. So I do not suspect him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-59"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011053","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7a5f8ed2077b723be4335a9b005becd41693e525d97aa9a68017c909adc04264","compact":"fb9c70b15ffb1d064e27abf2ded9975ee2ad9055038c9a68371a7180e75e451f","nasal":"180ed5b77c19d9127be7a0cfb30f6864296e2feca6e68e552e5bcbbd5643bf32"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-54","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":54,"english":"The wily can never come fearless and undisturbed. Nor were his words cunning. So I do not suspect him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.571,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-60"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011054","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"759418921911646eee427f9cb375996b214d04db0f9b4027d62e0e10668a56c2","compact":"af4feb256f6f156726cbb7a80376340ab316afd19aa6616a1eec06e9ab74a558","nasal":"0ebd8ba82fca7a4e7e020ca02d551d4db8d3279b67bb5aace646e0761f9569a2"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-55","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":55,"english":"It is not very easy to hide one's real nature. It manifests itself by force.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-61"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011055","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"725ddffb2ccee58963868046208c9916a04e462589a38e93235f18b92989c339","compact":"f8045d26b59559c28feb6ba48f7ddf6eaa49dffd8d5de3344008fcbbb9e0c798","nasal":"d648612583903e8d24d064658006f73789cafae9c4d72a2040c203e21be7bad5"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-56","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":56,"english":"So this action of Vibhīşana is not out of place or season. When accomplished it shall redound to his own interest.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.869,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-62"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011056","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"737ce63b899af64e963b669c0ab70e059d9693e28cc93785144024ac95e55a10","compact":"fa18150e54583014d51caed239273371e4173fcbbf28f27699ed6d8fa0307c48","nasal":"acbfdcea362a51f04d5ff4ee19c7e7db1d764fce1e12e9f2fed5fd92de132d31"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-57","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":57,"english":"Considering well your preparations for war and Ravana's vain conduct, hearing of Vah's destruction and Sugrīva's installation on the throne he has, impelled by his good sense, come here, desirous of gaining the kingdom. Taking these into account, it seems prudent to take him to our side.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.829,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-63"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011057","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"52ced83b17a0c352227ebc6947a70d528c6830ab7d752cfcf7be16b1ebe91631","compact":"6334d3963f449235a7959098b9224d96594f667622157c02f4dc33fc8b1a37e3","nasal":"6334d3963f449235a7959098b9224d96594f667622157c02f4dc33fc8b1a37e3"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-58","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":58,"english":"Considering well your preparations for war and Ravana's vain conduct, hearing of Vah's destruction and Sugrīva's installation on the throne he has, impelled by his good sense, come here, desirous of gaining the kingdom. Taking these into account, it seems prudent to take him to our side.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.493,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-63"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011058","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"044e64a943b457d33e344111376352c33cc6a94c9420851204e85b2389535522","compact":"eddd7a843287f0e5fd03fdfdc43d04a36d3488f338dfa5708cdccaffd605cfd0","nasal":"eddd7a843287f0e5fd03fdfdc43d04a36d3488f338dfa5708cdccaffd605cfd0"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-11-59","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":11,"verse":59,"english":"O you the foremost of the intelligent, I have spok thus considering him sincere. It now behove you to perform what you think proper.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.609,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-17-64"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6011059","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a90e35822cf9b3165fbc1188acb7ad6b59bd996dad2df87ed05269d05cb773ea","compact":"54556807353fec7b96be80e7796c76ed8b35e562fee82c10bec0f92ebb36684a","nasal":"54556807353fec7b96be80e7796c76ed8b35e562fee82c10bec0f92ebb36684a"}}]
